1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,056
First... who actually says no to you at the hospital desk?

2
00:00:04,056 --> 00:00:10,319
Most people think it's the insurance company sitting there evaluating your medical reports.

3
00:00:10,319 --> 00:00:12,991
But in reality, it's a middleman called a T-P-A...

4
00:00:12,991 --> 00:00:14,946
Third Party Administrator.

5
00:00:14,946 --> 00:00:18,318
Many think a T-P-A is a neutral government doctor.

6
00:00:18,318 --> 00:00:19,471
It is not.

7
00:00:19,471 --> 00:00:25,368
A T-P-A is a company hired and paid by the insurance company to process medical bills.

8
00:00:25,368 --> 00:00:30,605
In India, about seven out of every ten health claims are settled through T-P-As.

9
00:00:30,605 --> 00:00:38,201
Under I-R-D-A-I rules, no claim can be rejected without the approval of the insurance company's own claims review committee.

10
00:00:38,201 --> 00:00:42,205
But here are the three excuses you will often see on these letters.

11
00:00:42,205 --> 00:00:43,651
Excuse Number One.

12
00:00:43,651 --> 00:00:46,465
Non-disclosure of pre-existing condition.

13
00:00:46,465 --> 00:00:49,529
Suppose you were admitted for a broken leg or dengue.

14
00:00:49,529 --> 00:00:52,294
A junior doctor writes one line in your notes.

15
00:00:52,294 --> 00:00:54,462
Patient has mild blood pressure.

16
00:00:54,462 --> 00:00:56,531
The reviewer sees that one line.

17
00:00:56,531 --> 00:01:00,062
He opens your proposal form from five years ago, and says...

18
00:01:00,062 --> 00:01:01,697
You didn't declare blood pressure.

19
00:01:01,697 --> 00:01:03,350
Cashless denied.

20
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:07,765
Wait... does blood pressure cause a broken leg or a dengue infection?

21
00:01:07,765 --> 00:01:08,955
Of course not.

22
00:01:08,955 --> 00:01:13,165
But in the first five years of your policy, the company can still use it.

23
00:01:13,165 --> 00:01:15,512
After five years, the rule changes.

24
00:01:15,512 --> 00:01:16,891
Excuse Number Two.

25
00:01:16,891 --> 00:01:18,773
Not medically necessary.

26
00:01:18,773 --> 00:01:23,742
They say your treatment could have been done as an outpatient visit without staying in hospital.

27
00:01:23,742 --> 00:01:25,316
And Excuse Number Three.

28
00:01:25,316 --> 00:01:28,199
Room rent limit, and proportionate deduction.

29
00:01:28,199 --> 00:01:33,874
Say your policy allows a room of five thousand rupees a day, but you took an eight thousand rupee room.

30
00:01:33,874 --> 00:01:36,597
They don't just deduct the three thousand rupee difference.

31
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:43,267
They pay only five out of every eight rupees... on the surgery, doctor, and nursing charges too.

32
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:48,027
That is a cut of about thirty-seven percent on those charges.

33
00:01:48,027 --> 00:01:53,191
When a family sees that technical rejection letter, they feel completely helpless.

34
00:01:53,191 --> 00:01:55,602
They think the door is closed forever.

35
00:01:55,602 --> 00:01:56,699
It is not.

36
00:01:56,699 --> 00:02:00,032
A cashless denial... is NOT a claim rejection.

37
00:02:00,032 --> 00:02:02,671
Your legal right to the money is still alive.

